---
title: "JRN-006 Happy Path — Residential Mortgage Application"
---
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    actor PER001 as PER-001<br/>Personal Customer
    participant Channel as Channel<br/>Customer Portal / App (CAP-007)
    participant CAP001 as CAP-001 API<br/>Retail Banking
    participant CAP004 as CAP-004<br/>Risk Management
    participant CAP005 as CAP-005<br/>Compliance
    participant EB as Event Bus<br/>SVC-102
    participant Surveyor as External Surveyor
    participant Solicitor as Solicitor / Conveyancer
    participant CHAPS as CHAPS Network

    rect rgb(230, 245, 255)
        Note over PER001,CAP001: PH-009 — Mortgage Enquiry
        PER001->>Channel: Enter property details, deposit, income, product
        Channel->>CAP001: POST /mortgage-applications<br/>{ property_value: 390000, deposit: 97500,<br/>annual_income: 75000, product: 2yr_fixed }
        Note over CAP001: Internal: GET customer data (SVC-001 → SVC-002, same-capability)<br/>Create ENT-012 MortgageApplication (status: enquiry)<br/>Run affordability pre-check
        CAP001->>EB: Publish EVT-020 MortgageEnquiryStarted<br/>{ application_id, customer_id, property_value: 390000 }
        CAP001-->>Channel: 201 Created { application_id, pre_check_result: pass }
        Channel-->>PER001: Display affordability result
        EB-)CAP005: Consume EVT-020 MortgageEnquiryStarted
        Note over CAP005: Customer KYC current — no new CDD needed
        CAP005->>EB: Publish EVT-004 KYCClearanceGranted { customer_id, kkyc_current: true }
    end

    rect rgb(230, 255, 230)
        Note over PER001,CAP001: PH-010 — Decision in Principle (DIP) [Target: < 15 min]
        PER001->>Channel: Submit income/employment. Consent to soft credit check.
        Channel->>CAP001: POST /mortgage-applications/{id}/dip<br/>{ gross_income: 75000, employment_type: permanent,<br/>soft_credit_check_consent: true }
        Note over CAP001: Create ENT-013 AffordabilityAssessment (dip stage)<br/>Compute stress test (rate: 7%)<br/>Transition status: dip_pending
        CAP001->>EB: Publish EVT-022 CreditCheckRequested { application_id, type: soft }
        CAP001-->>Channel: 202 Accepted { polling_url }
        Channel-->>PER001: DIP in progress — check back shortly
        EB-)CAP004: Consume EVT-022 CreditCheckRequested (soft)
        Note over CAP004: Soft credit check — no bureau footprint<br/>Score: 720 — PASS
        CAP004->>EB: Publish EVT-023 CreditCheckCompleted { application_id, type: soft, result: pass, score: 720 }
        EB-)CAP001: Consume EVT-023 CreditCheckCompleted
        Note over CAP001: Affordability: PASS. Credit: PASS.<br/>Transition status: dip_issued<br/>Set dip_date, dip_expiry (+90 days)
        CAP001->>EB: Publish EVT-021 DIPIssued { application_id, dip_expiry }
        Note over EB: Route EVT-021 → Notifications (SVC-053):<br/>Email to customer: DIP certificate + ESIS document (valid 90 days)
    end

    rect rgb(255, 248, 220)
        Note over PER001,CAP001: PH-011 — Full Application
        PER001->>Channel: Submit full application. Upload payslips, P60, bank statements.<br/>Consent to hard credit check.
        Channel->>CAP001: POST /mortgage-applications/{id}/full-application<br/>{ documents: [payslips, p60, bank_statements],<br/>hard_credit_check_consent: true }
        Note over CAP001: Create ENT-013 AffordabilityAssessment (full_application stage)<br/>Transition status: full_application_submitted<br/>Set full_application_date
        CAP001->>EB: Publish EVT-022 CreditCheckRequested { application_id, type: hard }
        CAP001-->>Channel: 202 Accepted { status: full_application_submitted }
        EB-)CAP004: Consume EVT-022 CreditCheckRequested (hard)
        Note over CAP004: Hard credit check — bureau footprint recorded<br/>Full credit report. Score: 715 — PASS
        CAP004->>EB: Publish EVT-023 CreditCheckCompleted { application_id, type: hard, result: pass, score: 715 }
        EB-)CAP001: Consume EVT-023 CreditCheckCompleted
        Note over CAP001: Transition status: documents_complete
    end

    rect rgb(255, 235, 220)
        Note over CAP001,Surveyor: PH-012 — Valuation (desktop AVM — LTV 75%)
        Note over CAP001: Determine valuation type: desktop AVM<br/>Create ENT-014 PropertyValuation (status: instructed)<br/>Transition status: valuation_pending
        CAP001->>EB: Publish EVT-024 ValuationInstructed { application_id, type: desktop }
        CAP001->>Surveyor: Instruct AVM valuation (automated)
        Surveyor-->>CAP001: Valuation report: £385,000<br/>(purchase price £390,000 | down_valuation_flag: false)
        Note over CAP001: Update ENT-014 (status: completed, amount: £385,000)<br/>Recalculate LTV: 292,500/385,000 = 75.97%<br/>Transition status: valuation_complete
        CAP001->>EB: Publish EVT-025 ValuationCompleted<br/>{ application_id, amount: 385000, down_valuation: false, ltv: 75.97 }
    end

    rect rgb(240, 220, 255)
        Note over CAP001,EB: PH-013 — Underwriting (PER-055)
        Note over CAP001: Assign to PER-055 underwriter queue<br/>Transition status: underwriting<br/>PER-055 reviews full pack:<br/>Credit: 715 PASS | LTI: 3.8x (< 4.5x cap) PASS<br/>Affordability at 7% stress: PASS | LTV: 75.97% PASS<br/>Decision: APPROVE
        CAP001->>EB: Publish EVT-026 MortgageUnderwritingCompleted<br/>{ application_id, decision: approved }
    end

    rect rgb(255, 220, 220)
        Note over PER001,CAP001: PH-014 — Mortgage Offer
        Note over CAP001: Create ENT-015 MortgageOffer:<br/>amount: £292,500 @ 4.89%, 25 years<br/>expires: +6 months<br/>Transition status: offer_issued
        CAP001->>EB: Publish EVT-027 MortgageOfferIssued { application_id, offer_id }
        Note over EB: Route EVT-027 → Notifications (SVC-053):<br/>Email + Post: Mortgage Offer (7-day reflection period starts)
        Note over Solicitor: Mortgage Offer copy sent to Solicitor
        Note over PER001,Solicitor: 7-day reflection period elapses (MCOB 6.7)<br/>Customer reviews offer with solicitor
        PER001->>Channel: Accept mortgage offer
        Channel->>CAP001: POST /mortgage-applications/{id}/offer { acceptance_confirmed: true }
        Note over CAP001: Validate: accepted_date >= offer_date + 7 days<br/>Update ENT-015 (customer_accepted: true)<br/>Transition status: offer_accepted
        CAP001->>EB: Publish EVT-028 MortgageOfferAccepted { application_id, accepted_at }
        CAP001-->>Channel: 200 OK { status: offer_accepted }
        Channel-->>PER001: Offer accepted confirmation
    end

    rect rgb(220, 255, 240)
        Note over Solicitor,CHAPS: PH-015 — Completion
        Note over Solicitor: Completes conveyancing, Land Registry searches,<br/>exchange of contracts
        Solicitor->>CAP001: Requisition for funds (completion_date, CHAPS details)
        CAP001->>CHAPS: CHAPS payment instruction (£292,500 to solicitor)
        CHAPS-->>CAP001: Settlement confirmed { chaps_payment_reference }
        Note over CAP001: Create ENT-016 MortgageAccount:<br/>balance: £292,500 | payment: £1,683.42/month<br/>rate: 4.89% | term: 300 months | status: active<br/>Set up Bacs DD mandate<br/>Transition application status: completed
        CAP001->>EB: Publish EVT-029 MortgageCompleted { application_id, mortgage_account_id }
        CAP001->>EB: Publish EVT-030 MortgageAccountOpened<br/>{ mortgage_account_id, customer_id,<br/>balance: 292500, monthly_payment: 1683.42 }
        EB-)CAP001: Consume EVT-030 — update Customer product holdings (intra-CAP-001)
        Note over EB: Route EVT-030 → Notifications (SVC-053):<br/>Email + Post: Mortgage account open.<br/>Account details, payment schedule, first payment date.
        Note over PER001: Journey complete<br/>MortgageAccount active | Monthly payment: £1,683.42<br/>Bacs DD mandate active
    end
